## antenna: printed monopole extracted from the PcbBoard [doc-injected board → doc-extract]
  net ANT, 19 segments, feed OnEdge, ground infinite_image (0.50 λ along edge)
   · infinite PEC ground plane at the 'GND' pour edge (image theory): the coplanar pour (50.0 × 18.0 mm = 0.50 × 0.18 λ at 3000 MHz) is replaced by an infinite plane perpendicular to the antenna. Exact only for a pour large in wavelengths; a sub-wavelength pour shifts resonance and radiates from the ground currents too
   · free-space model: no substrate. FR-4 trace antennas resonate roughly 20–30 % BELOW a free-space prediction (docs/antenna-measurement-pack.md: f_meas/f_pred ≈ 1/√ε_eff, ε_eff ≈ 1.5–2 for a trace at a pour edge). Treat predicted frequencies as an upper bound; the substrate is recorded in `substrate` for the dielectric model (G7)
   · pour geometry is the zone's requested outline, not its filled copper (clearance cutouts are not seen)
   · traces → round wires of radius width/4 (zero-thickness strip equivalence); 1 wire elements, 19 segments, ≤ λ/60 at 3000 MHz
  resonance (Im Z = 0) 2357 MHz (free space; FR4 pulls it lower)
  S11 min -16.5 dB at 2400 MHz; at 2.44 GHz -15.2 dB

